From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: the shader set converts the recipe's task/mesh records too, keyed with this core's mesh state hash (EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_MESH=1), off by default

Switch: EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_MESH=1 (exact "1", read once). Needs EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET=1 and so
EDEN_UP_CANONICAL_KEYS=1. Off: nothing changes (same records, same file bytes, same stamp).

Why: the d4 cold start dropped all 2,874 task/mesh records of the recipe
("mesh-predicted-unsupported"), by design of the first port; that start asked for 59 mesh
pipelines (first_start.list, M rows), all translated on the GPU thread (18 ms each on average in
T151, up to 112 ms).

What a mesh pipeline key is here (ShaderCache::RefreshStages, VertexAttributeMaskOf): the task
program in the vertex B slot and the mesh program in the tessellation slot (a lone mesh program
in the vertex B slot); each of those two hashes is the lowered program hash XOR MeshStateHash =
CityHash64(mesh registers A, B, init, and the 80-byte pass-through header when the geometry slot
is on, else zeros) | 1; the drawing state is the usual 1,008 bytes, and with
EDEN_UP_CANONICAL_KEYS=1 its vertex attribute types are cleared (task/mesh programs have no vertex
input). Checked on the Mac against this console's vulkan_mesh.bin (602 of 602 records: key =
lowered ^ MeshStateHash of the record's own registers and header). The recipe holds every part:
its mesh facts carry the registers and the header (or flag 2 when there is none), its records
the per-slot XOR, and that XOR is this same hash for 2,868 of its 2,874 mesh records
(t158/recipe_check.py).

Why mesh keys did not repeat between sessions (0 of 97 in T151): the attribute types field
(FixedPipelineState +64). With canonical keys off (the T151 play env), a mesh pipeline's key keeps
whatever vertex attribute types the game last left in the registers; in this console's
vulkan_mesh.bin, 602 records are 175 keys once that field is cleared. EDEN_UP_CANONICAL_KEYS=1
clears it already (Fritchii v5.5's rule, in this tree since 0501): no new canonical form is
needed. Every one of d4's 59 M rows (canonical keys on) is a record of this console's earlier
sessions keyed that way. The init register (0x00802020 or 0x06419020) and the mask components bit
also differ between records, but they are drawing state and a switch, not session noise.

What, with the switch:
- Lower() lowers task and mesh programs too, as the vertex/tessellation slots lower them (128-byte
  header area, no geometry option); their read mask is 0.
- A task/mesh record is converted when, besides the usual checks, this core's mesh state hash
  made from the record's mesh fact equals the recipe's XOR in each task/mesh slot (and the other
  slots' XOR is 0); else dropped as "mesh-state-differs" (6 records). Those slots' hashes are the
  lowered hash XOR that state hash; the .programs sidecar keeps the plain lowered hashes.
- Task and mesh facts are stored whole; AppendEnvironment writes them as Serialize with mesh state
  does (tables, program header, registers, pass-through header, zeros when the fact has none),
  and ReadRecords reads every environment with mesh state (only task and mesh environments read
  it, so files of vertex and pixel records read as before).
- The stamp gets "mesh 1". One log line: how many converted records are task/mesh.
- The preparation does not take them without 0783.

T161s: applies after 0770-0772 (T157); the code is T158's, only the context lines are new.
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/shader_set.cpp b/src/video_core/shader_set.cpp
index 87f8601..2431e43 100644
--- a/src/video_core/shader_set.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/shader_set.cpp
@@ -201,6 +201,7 @@ std::string ExtractorLines() {
     lines += "records layout 3\n"; // each program's code once, with its hash (ReadRecords)
     // 0780: a set with compute records is another file (off: no line, the stamp as before).
     if (ComputeAsked()) lines += "compute 1\n";
+    if (MeshAsked()) lines += "mesh 1\n"; // 0782
     // EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_RECONVERT=<n> (a test aid): a number in the stamp, so a set made with
     // another number (or none) is converted again once, e.g. to time the conversion.
     if (const size_t again = SwitchNumber("EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_RECONVERT", 0); again != 0) {
@@ -294,7 +295,10 @@ std::optional<Lowered> Lower(const Guest& p, std::stop_token stop) {
     using namespace Shader::Ampere;
     // Ordinary graphics (vertex, pixel); with EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_COMPUTE=1 (0780) compute too.
     const bool compute = p.stage == 5 && ComputeAsked();
-    if (p.stage != 0 && p.stage != 4 && !compute) return {};
+    // 0782, EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_MESH=1: task and mesh programs, lowered as GraphicsEnvironment
+    // lowers them in the vertex and tessellation slots (128-byte header area, no geometry).
+    const bool mesh = (p.stage == 7 || p.stage == 8) && MeshAsked();
+    if (p.stage != 0 && p.stage != 4 && !compute && !mesh) return {};
     // A graphics program's code area starts with 128 bytes, the first 80 its program header
     // (GraphicsEnvironment lowers from +128). A native compute program has no header: the live
     // path lowers from its first byte and puts a zero header in front (ComputeEnvironment:
@@ -331,6 +335,9 @@ std::optional<Lowered> Lower(const Guest& p, std::stop_token stop) {
     // v3: the canonical key keeps only the attribute types the vertex program's header lists
     // (VideoCommon::GenericReadMask, as the live key is masked).
     out.read_mask = p.stage == 0 ? VideoCommon::GenericReadMask(sph) : ~0U;
+    if (mesh) {
+        out.read_mask = 0; // VertexAttributeMaskOf: task and mesh programs have no vertex input
+    }
     out.code.resize(sizeof(sph) / 8);
     std::memcpy(out.code.data(), &sph, sizeof(sph));
     for (u64 instruction : lowered.instructions) {
@@ -370,7 +377,37 @@ bool ComputeFactOk(const Facts& f, const Lowered& p) {
 /// What a records file keeps of a fact: graphics facts up to their tables' end (nothing follows
 /// them for the vertex and pixel stages), compute facts whole (0780: workgroup and shared memory).
 size_t StoredFactBytes(const Facts& f) {
-    return f.bytes.size() >= 76 && Load<u32>(f.bytes, 72) == 5 ? f.bytes.size() : f.tables_end;
+    if (f.bytes.size() < 76) return f.tables_end;
+    const u32 stage = Load<u32>(f.bytes, 72);
+    // 0782: task and mesh facts end with the mesh registers (and the pass-through header).
+    return stage == 5 || stage == 7 || stage == 8 ? f.bytes.size() : f.tables_end;
+}
+
+/// 0782: ShaderCache::MeshStateHash of a task/mesh pipeline from its mesh program's fact: the mesh
+/// registers A, B and init (12 bytes after the tables) and the pass-through header (80 bytes,
+/// absent from the fact when its flag 2 is set: then zero, as with no geometry slot).
+std::optional<u64> FactMeshStateHash(const Facts& f) {
+    if (f.tables_end + 12 > f.bytes.size()) return std::nullopt;
+    std::array<u8, 12 + 80> state{};
+    const size_t have = std::min<size_t>(state.size(), f.bytes.size() - f.tables_end);
+    if (have != 12 && have != state.size()) return std::nullopt;
+    std::memcpy(state.data(), f.bytes.data() + f.tables_end, have);
+    return Common::CityHash64(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(state.data()), state.size()) | 1;
+}
+
+/// 0782: where a fact's five answer tables end (counts at +8, entries of 8, 8, 12, 9, 12 bytes).
+size_t TablesEnd(std::span<const char> fact) {
+    static constexpr std::array<size_t, 5> widths{8, 8, 12, 9, 12};
+    size_t at = 76;
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < widths.size(); ++i) {
+        u64 count{};
+        std::memcpy(&count, fact.data() + 8 + i * 8, sizeof(count));
+        if (count > (fact.size() - at) / widths[i]) throw std::runtime_error("short shader data");
+        at += static_cast<size_t>(count) * widths[i];
+    }
+    if (fact.size() - at != 12 && fact.size() - at != 12 + 80)
+        throw std::runtime_error("mesh state size");
+    return at;
 }
 
 /// One environment as FileEnvironment::Deserialize reads it: the fact's bytes (up to its tables'
@@ -393,6 +430,16 @@ void AppendEnvironment(std::vector<char>& out, std::span<const char> fact,
     if (stage == 5) {
         return; // 0780: compute: the fact's workgroup and shared memory end it, no program header
     }
+    if (stage == 7 || stage == 8) {
+        // 0782: tables, the program header, then the mesh registers and the pass-through header
+        // (Serialize with mesh state); the fact holds the last two after its tables.
+        const size_t mesh_at = TablesEnd(fact);
+        out.resize(out.size() - (fact.size() - mesh_at));
+        out.insert(out.end(), code.begin(), code.begin() + 80);
+        out.insert(out.end(), fact.begin() + mesh_at, fact.end());
+        out.resize(out.size() + (12 + 80) - (fact.size() - mesh_at)); // a header left out: zero
+        return;
+    }
     out.insert(out.end(), code.begin(), code.begin() + 80); // graphics ProgramHeader is absent from facts
 }
 
@@ -470,6 +517,11 @@ bool ComputeAsked() {
     return asked;
 }
 
+bool MeshAsked() {
+    static const bool asked = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_MESH");
+    return asked;
+}
+
 bool Rest(std::stop_token stop, std::chrono::steady_clock::duration rest) {
     if (rest <= std::chrono::steady_clock::duration::zero()) {
         return !stop.stop_requested();
@@ -759,6 +811,7 @@ Outputs Prepare(u64 title, const std::filesystem::path& title_dir,
         std::unordered_set<u64> used_seen;
         size_t converted = 0;
         size_t compute_converted = 0; // 0780
+        size_t mesh_converted = 0;    // 0782
         u64 next_report = u64{512} << 20;
         std::vector<u8> used_fact(r.facts.size());
         for (const auto& p : r.records) {
@@ -798,10 +851,27 @@ Outputs Prepare(u64 title, const std::filesystem::path& title_dir,
                 absent |= !have.contains(r.programs[pi].fingerprint);
                 lower_failed |= !lowered[pi].has_value();
             }
-            if (mesh) { ++dropped["mesh-predicted-unsupported"]; continue; }
+            if (mesh && !MeshAsked()) { ++dropped["mesh-predicted-unsupported"]; continue; }
             if (absent) { ++dropped["fingerprint-not-found"]; continue; }
             if (lower_failed) { ++dropped["stage-or-lowering"]; continue; }
-            if (std::ranges::any_of(p.xors, [](u64 x) { return x != 0; })) {
+            // 0782: a task/mesh key's program hashes in the task/mesh slots carry the mesh state
+            // (ShaderCache::RefreshStages: unique hash ^ MeshStateHash). Ours is made from the
+            // mesh program's fact and must be the recipe's XOR in those slots, zero elsewhere.
+            std::array<u64, 6> mesh_xor{};
+            if (mesh) {
+                std::optional<u64> state_hash;
+                for (auto id : p.facts) {
+                    if (r.programs[r.facts[id].program].stage == 8) state_hash = FactMeshStateHash(r.facts[id]);
+                }
+                bool same = state_hash.has_value();
+                for (size_t s = 0; same && s < 6; ++s) {
+                    if (p.slots[s] == 0xff) continue;
+                    const auto stage = r.programs[r.facts[p.facts[p.slots[s]]].program].stage;
+                    mesh_xor[s] = stage == 7 || stage == 8 ? *state_hash : 0;
+                    same = p.xors[s] == mesh_xor[s];
+                }
+                if (!same) { ++dropped["mesh-state-differs"]; continue; }
+            } else if (std::ranges::any_of(p.xors, [](u64 x) { return x != 0; })) {
                 ++dropped["unexpected-hash-xor"]; continue;
             }
             std::array<u64, 6> hashes{};
@@ -812,10 +882,12 @@ Outputs Prepare(u64 title, const std::filesystem::path& title_dir,
             }
             if (!valid) { ++dropped["incompatible-facts"]; continue; }
             u32 read_mask = ~0U;
+            std::array<u64, 6> program_hashes{}; // without the mesh state (the .programs sidecar)
             for (size_t s = 0; s < 6; ++s) {
                 if (p.slots[s] == 0xff) continue;
                 const auto& program = *lowered[r.facts[p.facts[p.slots[s]]].program];
-                hashes[s] = program.hash;
+                hashes[s] = program.hash ^ mesh_xor[s];
+                program_hashes[s] = program.hash;
                 if (s == 1) read_mask = program.read_mask; // the vertex B slot
             }
             std::vector<u8> key;
@@ -834,8 +906,10 @@ Outputs Prepare(u64 title, const std::filesystem::path& title_dir,
                 LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan, "Shader set: converting: {} records, {} MB written, "
                          "{:.1f} s so far", converted, file.Written() >> 20, seconds());
             }
+            if (mesh) ++mesh_converted;
             for (size_t s = 0; s < 6; ++s) {
-                if (hashes[s] != 0 && used_seen.insert(hashes[s]).second) used_programs.push_back(hashes[s]);
+                if (program_hashes[s] != 0 && used_seen.insert(program_hashes[s]).second)
+                    used_programs.push_back(program_hashes[s]);
             }
         }
         size_t total_dropped = 0;
@@ -849,6 +923,10 @@ Outputs Prepare(u64 title, const std::filesystem::path& title_dir,
             LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan, "Shader set: EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_COMPUTE=1: {} of the converted records "
                      "are compute pipelines", compute_converted);
         }
+        if (MeshAsked()) {
+            LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan, "Shader set: EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_MESH=1: {} of the converted records "
+                     "are task/mesh pipelines", mesh_converted);
+        }
         if (!converted || stop.stop_requested()) return out;
         // The facts and the programs the records name, each once, and the trailer.
         const u64 facts_at = file.Written();
@@ -1091,7 +1169,9 @@ bool ReadRecords(
                 continue;
             }
             std::vector<FileEnvironment> envs(num_envs);
-            for (FileEnvironment& env : envs) env.Deserialize(in);
+            // With mesh state (0782): read only for task and mesh environments, so a file of
+            // vertex and pixel records reads as before.
+            for (FileEnvironment& env : envs) env.Deserialize(in, true);
             on_graphics(in, std::move(envs));
         }
         return true;
diff --git a/src/video_core/shader_set.h b/src/video_core/shader_set.h
index 6b635b0..f747003 100644
--- a/src/video_core/shader_set.h
+++ b/src/video_core/shader_set.h
@@ -115,6 +115,13 @@ void OverrideDuty(unsigned percent);
 /// before ("compute-predicted-unsupported") and the stamp is as before.
 [[nodiscard]] bool ComputeAsked();
 
+/// EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_MESH=1 (0782; exact "1", read once; off by default): the recipe's task/mesh
+/// records are converted too: their programs lowered as the vertex/tessellation slots lower them,
+/// their key's task/mesh slots XORed with this core's mesh state hash (made from the mesh fact and
+/// required to equal the recipe's XOR), their environments with mesh state. Off: dropped as before
+/// ("mesh-predicted-unsupported") and the stamp is as before.
+[[nodiscard]] bool MeshAsked();
+
 /// Sleeps `rest` unless the stop token is signalled first; false when it was.
 [[nodiscard]] bool Rest(std::stop_token stop, std::chrono::steady_clock::duration rest);
 
